    "q-69909": {
      "dom_id": "step-q69909",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the angle between $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})={120}^{∘}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
