    "q-67797": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67797",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the angle between $a=⟨-1,7,0⟩$ and $b=⟨3,6,-1⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place.",
      "worked_solution": "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 3+7\\cdot 6+0\\cdot (-1)}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{7}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{\\sqrt{50}\\cdot \\sqrt{46}} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{\\sqrt{2300}} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{10\\sqrt{23}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{39}{10\\sqrt{23}})≈{35.6}^{∘}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
