    "q-18321": {
      "dom_id": "step-q18321",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find the angle between $a=⟨1,-1,0⟩$ and $b=⟨0,1,-2⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place.",
      "worked_solution": "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}})≈{108.4}^{∘}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
