      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the angle between $a=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 6+6\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{6}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{100}\\cdot \\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{10\\cdot 7} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{35}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{6}{35})≈{80.13}^{∘}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
